WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.120
Captain Marvel will introduce Carol Danvers
to the Marvel Cinematic Universe on March

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.660
8th.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.540
Early screenings have received fairly positive
responses, and opening weekend projections

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:15.840
are anywhere from as low as $80 million to
the $150 to $180 million dollar range - and

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.040
who are we kidding you know why.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.670
Let's set all the other stuff aside and just
look at the character itself and what Captain

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:23.900
Marvel brings to the MCU.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:29.460
Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige confirmed
to Entertainment Weekly that Captain Marvel

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.460
is the most powerful hero the MCU has ever
seen.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.120
Considering the abilities we've seen from
some of the Avengers already, that's saying

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:37.660
quite a bit.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:43.280
With cosmic-level powers including super strength,
flight, and the capacity to survive the vacuum

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:48.900
of space, Captain Marvel's skill set is closer
to that of DC's Superman than anyone in the

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:49.520
MCU.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:54.340
Additionally, Captain Marvel can absorb any
kind of energy and release that energy as

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:56.780
concentrated blasts, usually from her hands.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:03.300
Captain Marvel and Avengers: Endgame are the
final films of Marvel's Phase 3, an era that

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.600
will have spanned ten films since 2016.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.060
Spider-Man: Far From Home will officially
kick off Phase 4 and a new direction for Marvel

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:11.680
Studios.

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:17.180
Marvel is known for unveiling their release
plans well in advance, but with Phase 4, they've

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.620
been slow to confirm production of upcoming
films.

00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:25.060
One reason for that may be the events of these
two movies and their world-shaking consequences

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:25.940
for the MCU.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:29.780
How does the world's most profitable film
franchise get bigger?

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.560
Speaking at an event for Ant-Man and the Wasp,
Kevin Feige clued us in on the direction the

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.240
MCU's Phase 4 will be taking.

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:37.540
He said:

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:41.999
"I love [cosmic stories] and that's why we
didn't wait very long to get that, I'd say.

00:01:41.999 --> 00:01:46.609
Thor was the beginning of that, Tesseract
in Cap as well […] I love it because I love

00:01:46.609 --> 00:01:49.929
space stuff and I love the kind of stories
you can tell."

00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:54.099
Sounds like Captain Marvel will likely be
the beginning of a major narrative shift to

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.500
the universal and the infinite.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:02.500
In Marvel Comics, the Eternals are an extraordinarily
powerful, near-immortal race of cosmic beings

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.360
who have existed for millions of years.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:05.840
Thanos is an Eternal.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.380
With Marvel's Phase 4 potentially shifting
to a future in the outer reaches of space,

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.420
beginning in earnest with Captain Marvel,
it's quite possible audiences will get some

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.180
Eternals in this movie.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.200
Marvel Studios has already confirmed that
an Eternals movie is in the works for Phase

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:21.740
4.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.640
Created by comic book legend Jack Kirby, the
Eternals and their enemies, the Deviants,

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:32.340
are two ancient alien races genetically engineered
by beings known as the Celestials.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.620
In the MCU, Kurt Russell's Ego the Living
Planet of Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 was

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.380
a Celestial.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.480
“We are forever.”

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.760
“Doesn't eternity get boring?”

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.480
“Not if you have a purpose, Peter.”

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:49.340
Eternals have special powers, well beyond
those of mortal men.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.700
It's implied that the Eternals, with names
closely resembling mythological gods, were

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.560
the true inspiration for those myths in ancient
times.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:03.160
If the mind of your inner nerd isn't completely
blown by just how cosmic the MCU is about

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:08.280
to get, starting with Captain Marvel then
you have a Celestial-level tolerance for awesomeness.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:15.520
At San Diego Comic Con in 2017, diehard Marvel
fans were treated to some sweet fan service

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:20.280
when Marvel announced that Captain Marvel
would be the first MCU appearance of the Skrulls.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.920
The Skrulls are a race of shape-shifting aliens
that have been around in the comics since

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:25.580
the early days.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.270
The ante was upped even more with the news
that the film would include a narrative thread

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:34.720
of the Kree-Skrull War, a bitter intergalactic
feud between the two races first introduced

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.940
to comics in 1971.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.770
The Kree-Skrull conflict promises to be an
important aspect of world building for the

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:43.700
ever-expanding Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.340
Speaking to Entertainment Weekly in a new
featurette, Co-director Anna Boden said:

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:54.100
"Carol [Danvers] knows the Skrulls have infiltrated
Earth, and it kind of creates this sense of

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:54.620
paranoia.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.880
The Skrulls are after something, and part
of the mystery of the movie is Carol trying

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.800
to figure out what they're after, and getting
it before they do."

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.220
In the Endgame trailer, we see Tony Stark
trapped in a spacecraft that's out of fuel

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.060
and low on oxygen.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.960
Theories abound about who will be the one
to save Stark.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:16.440
One theory that has gained steam is the idea
of Captain Marvel coming to Iron Man's rescue.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:21.960
Some look to the post-credits scene in Infinity
War, in which Nick Fury pages Carol Danvers

00:04:21.969 --> 00:04:26.740
just before getting dusted, as evidence of
the possibility of a Captain Marvel/Iron Man

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.220
team-up on deck for Endgame.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.120
One intriguing fan theory has outlined an
interesting role Nick Fury could play in Captain

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:33.640
Marvel.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:39.040
An astute Redditor made waves by predicting
that '90s Nick Fury "will be shown or made

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.420
aware of the future," and be persuaded to
arrange the events that we've witnessed on

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.360
screen so far.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.460
In other words, everything that has happened
in the MCU had to happen just the way it did

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:53.000
for the good guys to have any chance at ultimately
defeating Thanos.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.660
With that kind of foresight, Fury never needed
both eyes after all.

00:04:56.669 --> 00:05:05.710
"If you want to stay ahead of me, Mr. Secretary,
you need to keep both eyes open."

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:10.580
The Supreme Intelligence is a little-known
but classic cosmic entity created by Stan

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.460
Lee and Jack Kirby.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.100
The character first appeared in a 1967 issue
of Fantastic Four.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.419
This artificial intelligence was created by
the Kree to help create a Cosmic Cube, as

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.000
their enemies the Skrulls had done.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.840
In the MCU, the Cosmic Cube is also known
as the Tesseract, or more recently, the Space

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.940
Stone on Thanos' Infinity Gauntlet.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:36.099
After much speculation, Annette Bening recently
revealed her role in Captain Marvel to be

00:05:36.099 --> 00:05:40.809
none other than the Supreme Intelligence,
who promises to be unlike any other character

00:05:40.809 --> 00:05:43.180
we've met in the Marvel Cinematic Universe
so far.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.260
During an interview on The Late Show with
Stephen Colbert, Bening described her character

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.900
as "a god-like entity."

00:05:48.909 --> 00:05:54.960
"The artificial intelligence which consists
of the greatest intellects of the Kree people

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.699
for the last million years."

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:00.939
Speaking to The Hollywood Reporter, Marvel
Studios President Kevin Feige discussed the

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:04.680
prominent role female characters are going
to play in Phase 4 and beyond.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:08.680
Discussing the notion of making more movies
with female leads, Feige said:

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.240
"We feel like it'll be the first of many.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:14.120
There were a lot of men in that initial run
of Avengers."

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:19.840
Indeed, the next female-driven MCU project
is reportedly already in the works.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:24.340
Black Widow, starring Scarlett Johansson,
is rumored to begin filming in 2019.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:30.740
The movie will reportedly be released in late
2020 or early 2021, with additional details

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:34.800
likely becoming available once Phase 4 begins
with Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:40.380
Captain Marvel wants to tell an origin story,
but in a completely different way.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:43.200
Speaking to Mashable, producer Jonathan Schwartz
said:

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:47.860
"In many ways, it's a classic Marvel origin
story but told in reverse, structurally.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:53.700
You meet her as an awesome badass superpowered
space hero, and then learn who the human is

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:54.660
behind that aspect of herself."

00:06:55.969 --> 00:07:00.400
The story begins on the planet Hala, where
she is deeply involved in the Kree-Skrull

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:05.320
War, battling on the side of the Kree people,
and in full control of her potent superpowers.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:10.400
The audience is then taken back to Carol Danvers'
home planet of Earth, where the origin story

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.400
proper begins.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:16.360
Once there, Carol discovers her past may hold
the key to her struggles in the present.

